  "id": "COMPOUND:29957 - PROTEIN:6151",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which 4'-O-methylmelanettin may interact with Ataxin-2, through a series of molecular interactions involving the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3. This transporter is targeted by oleamide and ancistrobenomine A, both of which are metabolites of 4'-O-methylmelanettin. The presence of multiple pathways pointing to the same target, with consistent scores across different paths, indicates a plausible and well-supported relationship. The core mechanism appears to involve the modulation of the H(+)/Cl(-) exchange transporter 3, which may influence the activity of Ataxin-2. The integration of these pathways suggests that 4'-O-methylmelanettin could act as a modulator of the transporter, potentially affecting Ataxin-2 function. The evidence is robust and consistent, supporting a mechanistic link between the compound and Ataxin-2.",
